{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788280372,"nonce":"7yMm+UBYyPckqEylV1nBu2XUgws=","message":"BENCH FINDING — THIS ISSUE'S `wiped[]` BULLET DESCRIBES A CASE THE GAME REFUSES\nBEFORE THE WIPE PATH RUNS. Session 16, 2026-09-01, assembly `8b804c5`.\n\nThe bullet reads:\n\n\u003e `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", buildable:false}` onto a rock wall: placed, and\n\u003e `wiped[0]` names the rock with `removal:\"mine\"`.\n\n**It cannot happen.** `Verse/GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` walks\n`GenAdj.OccupiedRect(...)` and inside that loop tests\n\n    if (!c.Walkable(map)) { return false; }\n\n— on **`c`, the CENTRE cell**, not on the loop variable `item`. (The same\nstatement block tests `item.InBounds` and `map.edificeGrid[item]` correctly, so\nthe centre-keying is a vanilla quirk rather than my misreading; `WhyNoSpawn`\nalready documents it for the `SpawningWipes` scan on the next line.) A rock wall\nmakes the centre unwalkable, so the call returns false **before**\n`canWipeEdifices` is consulted and long before `WipeExistingThings` could run.\n\nMeasured four ways on a live bench, every one refused with *\"the cell is not\nwalkable\"*:\n\n- `Wall` onto a `Wall`\n- `SimpleResearchBench` onto a `Wall`\n- `Wall` onto a spawned `Sandstone` rock wall — the bullet's own case\n- (and the fifth attempt, `Wall` onto a live blueprint, PLACED and reported\n  `wiped: []` — correctly, because the blueprint survived alongside it;\n  `SpawningWipes` does not name that pair)\n\nSo `wiped[]` is published and honest — `[]` on a successful spawn that erased\nnothing, `null` on a refusal — but **I could not construct a case that populates\nit**, and the acceptance's own example is not one.\n\n\nIt does NOT mean the field is pointless. `canWipeEdifices:true` genuinely does\nskip the `edificeGrid` check, so the wipe path is reachable in principle —\n`WipeMode.VanishOrMoveAside` is real and `WipeWatch` is wired to it. What the\nwalkable-centre test does is make the reachable set much smaller than this issue\nassumes: the occupant has to leave the CENTRE cell walkable while still being\nsomething `SpawningWipes` names.\n\nTwo consequences worth deciding rather than discovering later:\n\n1. **Reword the bullet** to a case that can actually occur, or state plainly\n   that `wiped[]` is a guard against a path the vanilla gate rarely admits and\n   that an empty list is the expected result. As written, the bullet cannot be\n   satisfied and a future session will burn an afternoon on it — I burned part\n   of one.\n2. **The centre-keyed `Walkable` is worth its own note wherever siting is\n   documented.** It means \"can this building go here\" has a vanilla answer that\n   depends on one cell of the footprint rather than all of them, which is\n   surprising in exactly the direction that produces false refusals for\n   multi-cell defs whose centre happens to be occupied.\n\nEverything else on this issue is proven live and is recorded on the issue and in\n`accept/runs/s16-20260901/`: `buildable:true` refuses what the god-hand allows\n(*\"Identical thing already exists here.\"* — a `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` check\n`CanSpawnAt` does not have), and `site-audit` returned `hit_count: 2` against a\ndeliberately staged pair of interaction-overlapping benches, each with the\ngame's own sentence.","files":null}]}